IMPORT prelude

-- Washington capital gains tax, chapter 82.87 RCW -- what an individual meets: who is a resident (RCW 82.87.020(11)), which
-- sales are exempt (82.87.050), which gains are allocated to Washington (82.87.100(1)), the adjusted capital gain
-- (82.87.020(1)), the deductions (82.87.060: the standard deduction, the family-owned small business deduction 82.87.070, the
-- charitable deduction 82.87.080), the tax at 7 percent plus 2.9 percent above $1,000,000 (82.87.040), the credits for tax
-- paid to another jurisdiction (82.87.100(2)) and for business and occupation tax (82.87.160), joint and separate returns
-- (82.87.120(1)-(2)), and three duties with deadlines: file by the federal due date (or the matched extension), pay by the
-- original due date regardless of extension, and amend within 90 days of a final federal change (82.87.110(1), (3), (5), (8)),
-- with the late-filing penalty (82.87.110(6)).
--
-- Washington levies no tax on wages or other ordinary income: this chapter is the one tax on an individual's income. NOTES.md
-- records that finding.
--
-- SEAT: the individual (or married couple) who sells stocks, bonds or other long-term capital assets. "Is this sale taxed? Is
-- the gain allocated to Washington? How much do I owe? Must I file, and by when?"
--
-- Edition: chapter 82.87 RCW as printed on app.leg.wa.gov (full-chapter page), retrieved 2026-10-24 (UTC), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/rcw-82-87.txt (unofficial). Includes 2026 c 191 and 2025 c 409, c 421.
--
-- ANNUAL AMOUNTS. The standard deduction ($250,000 printed), the charitable donation floor ($250,000) and cap ($100,000) and the
-- family-owned business revenue ceiling ($10,000,000) are adjusted each October by the Department of Revenue (82.87.150) and
-- published on its website, which is not deposited: they are INPUTS whose @desc names the printed figure. The $1,000,000
-- threshold of the 2.9 percent tax is not an "applicable amount" and is not adjusted (NOTES.md finding 3).
--
-- FEDERAL INPUTS. Federal net long-term capital gain (as defined in 82.87.020(3)) is a federal figure (subjects/us/
-- internal-revenue-code-of-1986/; cross-folder IMPORT is not possible).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Distribution of revenue (82.87.030), criminal penalties (82.87.140), brokers' 1099-B duties (82.87.170),
-- administration under chapter 82.32 RCW (late-payment interest and penalties are in 82.32, not deposited), the exemption
-- valuation of 82.87.050(2) (asked as an amount), the 82.87.110(6)(b), (7) waivers (asked as a fact), the trust rules of
-- 82.87.040(4)(b)(ii), and allocation between spouses filing separately (82.87.120(4)(b): the share is asked).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Washington capital gains tax -- chapter 82.87 RCW`

§§ `The parties and the actions`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the Department of Revenue`

DECLARE `Action` IS ONE OF
    `file the capital gains return with a copy of the federal return`
    `pay the capital gains tax`
    `file an amended capital gains return`

§§ `RCW 82.87.020(11) -- resident`

-- 82.87.020(11)(a): "'Resident' means an individual: (i) Who is domiciled in this state during the taxable year, unless the
-- individual (A) maintained no permanent place of abode in this state during the entire taxable year, (B) maintained a permanent
-- place of abode outside of this state during the entire taxable year, and (C) spent in the aggregate not more than 30 days of
-- the taxable year in this state; or (ii) Who is not domiciled in this state during the taxable year, but maintained a place of
-- abode and was physically present in this state for more than 183 days during the taxable year." (b): "'day' means a calendar
-- day or any portion of a calendar day."
GIVEN `domiciled in Washington in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `kept no permanent place of abode in Washington all year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `kept a permanent place of abode outside Washington all year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days in Washington` IS A NUMBER
      `kept a place of abode in Washington` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a resident under RCW 82.87.020(11)` IF
    IF `domiciled in Washington in the year`
    THEN NOT (    `kept no permanent place of abode in Washington all year`
              AND `kept a permanent place of abode outside Washington all year`
              AND `days in Washington` AT MOST 30)
    ELSE `kept a place of abode in Washington` AND `days in Washington` GREATER THAN 183

§§ `RCW 82.87.050 -- exempt sales`

-- 82.87.050: "This chapter does not apply to the sale or exchange of: (1) All real estate transferred by deed ...; (2) An interest
-- in a privately held entity only to the extent that any long-term capital gain ... is directly attributable to the real estate
-- owned directly by such entity; (3) Assets held under a retirement savings account ...; (4) Assets pursuant to, or under
-- imminent threat of, condemnation proceedings ...; (5) Cattle, horses, or breeding livestock if ... more than 50 percent of the
-- taxpayer's gross income ... is from farming or ranching; (6) Property depreciable under ... Sec. 167(a)(1) ... or that
-- qualifies for expensing under ... Sec. 179; (7) Timber, timberland, or ... dividends and distributions from real estate
-- investment trusts derived from gains from the sale or exchange of timber and timberland; (8)(a) Commercial fishing
-- privileges ...; (9) Goodwill received from the sale of an auto dealership".
DECLARE `What was sold` IS ONE OF
    `real estate transferred by a recorded instrument`
    `an interest in a privately held entity, to the extent of its directly owned real estate`
    `assets in a retirement account`
    `assets taken or under imminent threat of condemnation`
    `cattle, horses or breeding livestock`
    `depreciable or section 179 property`
    `timber or timberland, or REIT distributions from them`
    `commercial fishing privileges`
    `goodwill of a licensed auto dealership`
    `stocks, bonds or other long-term capital assets`

GIVEN `what was sold` IS A `What was sold`
      `more than half my gross income is from farming or ranching` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is exempt under RCW 82.87.050` IF
    CONSIDER `what was sold`
    WHEN `cattle, horses or breeding livestock` THEN `more than half my gross income is from farming or ranching`
    WHEN `stocks, bonds or other long-term capital assets` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `RCW 82.87.100(1) -- allocation to Washington`

-- 82.87.100(1)(a): gains or losses from tangible personal property are allocated to Washington "if the property was located in
-- this state at the time of the sale or exchange", or, if not, where "(i) The property was located in the state at any time
-- during the taxable year ... or the immediately preceding taxable year; (ii) The taxpayer was a resident at the time ...; and
-- (iii) The taxpayer is not subject to the payment of an income or excise tax legally imposed on the long-term capital gains or
-- losses by another taxing jurisdiction." (b): gains from intangible personal property "are allocated to this state if the
-- taxpayer was domiciled in this state at the time the sale or exchange occurred."
GIVEN `the property is intangible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `domiciled in Washington at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `located in Washington at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `located in Washington this year or last` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resident at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `taxed on the gain by another jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gain is allocated to Washington` IF
    IF `the property is intangible`
    THEN `domiciled in Washington at the time of the sale`
    ELSE    `located in Washington at the time of the sale`
         OR (    `located in Washington this year or last`
             AND `a resident at the time of the sale`
             AND NOT (`taxed on the gain by another jurisdiction`))

§§ `RCW 82.87.020(1), 82.87.040, 82.87.060 -- the tax`

-- 82.87.020(1): "'Adjusted capital gain' means federal net long-term capital gain" plus long-term losses (and loss carryovers)
-- from sales that are exempt or not allocated to Washington, and from before 2022, plus section 1256 long-term gains or losses,
-- "Less any amount of long-term capital gain from a sale or exchange that is not allocated to Washington ... [or] that is exempt".
-- The person states the federal figure and the two totals.
DECLARE `Capital gains facts` HAS
    `federal net long-term capital gain`                         IS A NUMBER
    `long-term losses from exempt or unallocated sales, and earlier carryovers, included in it` IS A NUMBER
    `long-term gains from exempt or unallocated sales included in it` IS A NUMBER
    `section 1256 long-term gain or loss not already included`   IS A NUMBER
    `standard deduction for the year`                            IS A NUMBER  -- 82.87.060(1): $250,000 printed, adjusted
    `share of the standard deduction on this return`             IS A NUMBER  -- 1, or a spouse's agreed share (82.87.120(4))
    `family-owned small business deduction`                      IS A NUMBER  -- 82.87.070, as an amount
    `donations to qualified Washington organisations`            IS A NUMBER
    `charitable floor for the year`                              IS A NUMBER  -- 82.87.080(1): $250,000 printed, adjusted
    `charitable cap for the year`                                IS A NUMBER  -- 82.87.080(2): $100,000 printed, adjusted
    `amounts the state may not tax`                              IS A NUMBER  -- 82.87.060(2)
    `taxable year`                                               IS A NUMBER

GIVEN f IS A `Capital gains facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the adjusted capital gain of` f MEANS
    `the additions` MINUS f's `long-term gains from exempt or unallocated sales included in it`
    WHERE
        `the additions` MEANS sum (LIST f's `federal net long-term capital gain`,
                                        f's `long-term losses from exempt or unallocated sales, and earlier carryovers, included in it`,
                                        f's `section 1256 long-term gain or loss not already included`)

-- 82.87.080(1)-(2): the amount donated "in excess of the minimum qualifying charitable donation amount", which "may not exceed
-- $100,000".
GIVEN f IS A `Capital gains facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the charitable deduction of` f MEANS
    min (f's `charitable cap for the year`) (max 0 (f's `donations to qualified Washington organisations` MINUS f's `charitable floor for the year`))

-- 82.87.060: "a taxpayer may deduct from his or her Washington capital gains: (1) A standard deduction of $250,000 per
-- individual, or in the case of spouses or domestic partners, their combined standard deduction is limited to $250,000,
-- regardless of whether they file joint or separate returns ...; (2) Amounts that the state is prohibited from taxing ...;
-- (3) [the family-owned small business deduction]; and (4) Charitable donations".
-- 82.87.020(16): "'Washington capital gains' means an individual's adjusted capital gain, as modified in RCW 82.87.060".
GIVEN f IS A `Capital gains facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Washington capital gains of` f MEANS
    `the adjusted capital gain of` f MINUS `the deductions of` f

GIVEN f IS A `Capital gains facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deductions of` f MEANS
    sum (LIST f's `standard deduction for the year` TIMES f's `share of the standard deduction on this return`,
              f's `amounts the state may not tax`,
              f's `family-owned small business deduction`,
              `the charitable deduction of` f)

-- 82.87.040(1)(a): the tax "equals seven percent multiplied by an individual's Washington capital gains"; (b) "Beginning
-- January 1, 2025, an additional ... 2.90 percent multiplied by the portion of an individual's Washington capital gains
-- exceeding $1,000,000." (3): "If an individual's Washington capital gains are less than zero ... no tax is due".
GIVEN `Washington capital gains` IS A NUMBER
      `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the RCW 82.87.040 tax on` `Washington capital gains` `taxable year` MEANS
    IF `Washington capital gains` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE (`Washington capital gains` TIMES 7%) PLUS `additional`
    WHERE
        `additional` MEANS IF `taxable year` AT LEAST 2025
                           THEN (max 0 (`Washington capital gains` MINUS 1000000)) TIMES 2.9%
                           ELSE 0

-- 82.87.100(2)(a): a nonrefundable credit, "the lesser of: (i) The total amount of tax due under this chapter derived from such
-- capital assets; or (ii) the total amount of tax paid to the other taxing jurisdiction". 82.87.160: a nonrefundable credit equal
-- to the business and occupation tax on the same sale, from tax year 2025, not above the tax due.
GIVEN `tax before credits` IS A NUMBER
      `Washington tax derived from assets taxed elsewhere` IS A NUMBER
      `tax paid to the other jurisdiction` IS A NUMBER
      `business and occupation tax on the same sales` IS A NUMBER
      `taxable year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax after credits` `tax before credits` `Washington tax derived from assets taxed elsewhere` `tax paid to the other jurisdiction` `business and occupation tax on the same sales` `taxable year` MEANS
    max 0 ((`tax before credits` MINUS `other state credit`) MINUS `b and o credit`)
    WHERE
        `other state credit` MEANS min `Washington tax derived from assets taxed elsewhere` `tax paid to the other jurisdiction`
        `b and o credit`     MEANS IF `taxable year` AT LEAST 2025 THEN `business and occupation tax on the same sales` ELSE 0

§§ `RCW 82.87.110 -- returns, payment, amendment`

-- 82.87.110(1)(a): "taxpayers owing tax under this chapter must file ... a return with the department on or before the date the
-- taxpayer's federal income tax return for the taxable year is required to be filed." (5): with evidence of a federal extension
-- given by the due date, "the taxpayer is entitled to the same extension of time for filing ... An extension ... is not an
-- extension of time to pay". (3): "pay any tax due thereon ... on or before the date fixed for the filing of the return,
-- regardless of any filing extension." Counted in days from the end of the taxable year.
GIVEN `days to the federal due date` IS A NUMBER
      `days to the extended due date, if the federal extension was shown in time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to file the capital gains return` `days to the federal due date` `days to the extended due date, if the federal extension was shown in time` MEANS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `file the capital gains return with a copy of the federal return`
    WITHIN max `days to the federal due date` `days to the extended due date, if the federal extension was shown in time`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "capital gains return not filed by the due date or extension: 5% of the tax a month, up to 25% (RCW 82.87.110(6))"

GIVEN `days to the federal due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to pay the capital gains tax` `days to the federal due date` MEANS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `pay the capital gains tax`
    WITHIN `days to the federal due date`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "capital gains tax not paid by the original due date; a filing extension does not extend payment (RCW 82.87.110(3), (5))"

-- 82.87.110(8): where the federal return "is changed in a manner that is final" and the change affects Washington capital gains
-- or the tax, "the taxpayer must amend"; (b) "If the return is not amended ... within 90 days of the federal income tax return
-- change becoming final, the department must assess on the 91st day a penalty" of 5 percent a month, up to 25 percent.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Action`
`my duty to amend after a federal change` MEANS
    PARTY  `the taxpayer`
    MUST   `file an amended capital gains return`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "no amended return within 90 days of the federal change becoming final: penalty from the 91st day (RCW 82.87.110(8)(b))"

-- 82.87.110(6)(a): "five percent of the tax due ... for each month or portion of a month that the return remains unfiled. The
-- total penalty ... may not exceed 25 percent of the tax due". (b): the Department "must waive or cancel" the penalty if the
-- failure was due to circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control, or the taxpayer filed on time in the preceding five years and
-- was not contacted for enforcement (asked as one fact).
GIVEN `tax due` IS A NUMBER
      `months or part months unfiled` IS A NUMBER
      `a waiver applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late filing penalty` `tax due` `months or part months unfiled` `a waiver applies` MEANS
    IF `a waiver applies`
    THEN 0
    ELSE min (`tax due` TIMES 25%) (`tax due` TIMES 5% TIMES `months or part months unfiled`)

§ `Questions for the seller`

§§ `Is my sale taxed in Washington?`

@export Does Washington tax my income from wages or other ordinary income? (No: chapter 82.87 RCW taxes only long-term capital gains.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Washington tax my wages` IF FALSE

@export Am I a Washington resident for the capital gains tax (RCW 82.87.020(11))?
GIVEN `I was domiciled in Washington during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Washington was your domicile (permanent legal home) at any time during the taxable year
      `I kept no permanent home in Washington all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintained no permanent place of abode in Washington during the entire year
      `I kept a permanent home outside Washington all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintained a permanent place of abode outside Washington during the entire year
      `days I was in Washington` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days (any part of a day counts) you were in Washington during the year
      `I kept a place of abode in Washington` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintained a place of abode in Washington during the year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a Washington resident for capital gains tax` IF
    `is a resident under RCW 82.87.020(11)` `I was domiciled in Washington during the year` `I kept no permanent home in Washington all year` `I kept a permanent home outside Washington all year` `days I was in Washington` `I kept a place of abode in Washington`

@export Is the sale of this asset exempt from Washington's capital gains tax (RCW 82.87.050)?
GIVEN `what I sold` IS A `What was sold` @desc What was sold or exchanged: real estate; an interest in a private entity (to the extent of its real estate); retirement account assets; condemned property; livestock; depreciable or section 179 property; timber; commercial fishing privileges; auto dealership goodwill; or stocks, bonds or other long-term capital assets
      `more than half my gross income is from farming or ranching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For livestock only: whether more than 50 percent of your gross income for the year (including capital gains) is from farming or ranching
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my sale exempt from Washington capital gains tax` IF
    `the sale is exempt under RCW 82.87.050` `what I sold` `more than half my gross income is from farming or ranching`

@export Is the gain on this sale allocated to Washington (RCW 82.87.100(1))?
GIVEN `the asset is intangible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the asset is intangible personal property, such as stocks, bonds or fund shares (true), or tangible personal property such as art or equipment (false)
      `I was domiciled in Washington when I sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Washington was your domicile at the time of the sale
      `the asset was in Washington when I sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For tangible property: whether it was located in Washington at the time of the sale
      `the asset was in Washington this year or last` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For tangible property: whether it was in Washington at any time during the year of sale or the year before
      `I was a resident when I sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Washington resident at the time of the sale
      `another jurisdiction taxes the gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you must pay another state's or country's income or excise tax on this gain
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my gain allocated to Washington` IF
    `the gain is allocated to Washington` `the asset is intangible` `I was domiciled in Washington when I sold it` `the asset was in Washington when I sold it` `the asset was in Washington this year or last` `I was a resident when I sold it` `another jurisdiction taxes the gain`

§§ `How much do I owe?`

@export How much Washington capital gains tax do I owe for the year (RCW 82.87.020, .040, .060-.080, .100(2), .160)?
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable year, for example 2026
      `my federal net long-term capital gain` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net long-term capital gain for federal income tax purposes, worked out as if IRC ss 55-59, 164, 1256, 1400Z-1 and 1400Z-2 did not exist, in US dollars (joint, if you file jointly)
      `losses from exempt or non-Washington sales included in it` IS A NUMBER @desc Long-term losses (and loss carryovers) included in that figure that come from exempt sales, sales not allocated to Washington, or sales before 2022, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `gains from exempt or non-Washington sales included in it` IS A NUMBER @desc Long-term gains included in that figure that come from exempt sales (real estate, retirement accounts and the others) or sales not allocated to Washington, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `section 1256 long-term gain or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Long-term gain (or loss, negative) on section 1256 contracts held more than a year, not already in the federal figure; 0 if none
      `the standard deduction for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The capital gains standard deduction for the year as published by the Department of Revenue; the statute prints 250000
      `my share of the standard deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 if you are single or file jointly; if you and your spouse or domestic partner file separately, your agreed share of the one combined deduction (for example 0.5)
      `my family-owned small business deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The adjusted capital gain from selling substantially all of a qualified family-owned small business (RCW 82.87.070), in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my donations to qualified Washington charities` IS A NUMBER @desc What you gave during the year to charities principally directed and managed in Washington, in US dollars
      `the charitable floor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum qualifying charitable donation amount for the year as published by the Department of Revenue; the statute prints 250000
      `the charitable cap for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum charitable donation deduction for the year as published by the Department of Revenue; the statute prints 100000
      `the Washington tax on assets also taxed elsewhere` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of this tax that comes from capital assets in another state or country that also taxed the gain, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `the tax I paid the other jurisdiction` IS A NUMBER @desc The income or excise tax you paid that other state or country on those gains, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `business and occupation tax on the same sales` IS A NUMBER @desc Washington business and occupation tax charged on the same sales (credit from 2025), in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much Washington capital gains tax do I owe` `the taxable year` `my federal net long-term capital gain` `losses from exempt or non-Washington sales included in it` `gains from exempt or non-Washington sales included in it` `section 1256 long-term gain or loss` `the standard deduction for the year` `my share of the standard deduction` `my family-owned small business deduction` `my donations to qualified Washington charities` `the charitable floor for the year` `the charitable cap for the year` `the Washington tax on assets also taxed elsewhere` `the tax I paid the other jurisdiction` `business and occupation tax on the same sales` MEANS
    `the tax after credits` (`the RCW 82.87.040 tax on` (`the Washington capital gains of` `facts`) `the taxable year`) `the Washington tax on assets also taxed elsewhere` `the tax I paid the other jurisdiction` `business and occupation tax on the same sales` `the taxable year`
    WHERE
        `facts` MEANS `Capital gains facts` WITH
            `federal net long-term capital gain`                         IS `my federal net long-term capital gain`
            `long-term losses from exempt or unallocated sales, and earlier carryovers, included in it` IS `losses from exempt or non-Washington sales included in it`
            `long-term gains from exempt or unallocated sales included in it` IS `gains from exempt or non-Washington sales included in it`
            `section 1256 long-term gain or loss not already included`   IS `section 1256 long-term gain or loss`
            `standard deduction for the year`                            IS `the standard deduction for the year`
            `share of the standard deduction on this return`             IS `my share of the standard deduction`
            `family-owned small business deduction`                      IS `my family-owned small business deduction`
            `donations to qualified Washington organisations`            IS `my donations to qualified Washington charities`
            `charitable floor for the year`                              IS `the charitable floor for the year`
            `charitable cap for the year`                                IS `the charitable cap for the year`
            `amounts the state may not tax`                              IS 0  -- 82.87.060(2): not asked (a placeholder)
            `taxable year`                                               IS `the taxable year`

§§ `Must I file, and by when?`

@export Must I file a Washington capital gains return (RCW 82.87.110(1))? Only taxpayers who owe the tax must.
GIVEN `the tax I owe` IS A NUMBER @desc The Washington capital gains tax you owe for the year, in US dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a Washington capital gains return` IF
    `the tax I owe` GREATER THAN 0

@export Must my spouse and I file a joint Washington capital gains return (RCW 82.87.120(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `we file a joint federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your federal income tax liabilities are determined on a joint federal return for the year
      `we are state registered domestic partners who choose to file jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are Washington state registered domestic partners who choose to file a joint Washington return although you filed separate federal returns
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we file a joint capital gains return` IF
    `we file a joint federal return` OR `we are state registered domestic partners who choose to file jointly`

@export How much is the Washington penalty for filing my capital gains return late (RCW 82.87.110(6))?
GIVEN `the tax due for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The capital gains tax due for the year, in US dollars
      `months or part months the return was late` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months, counting any part of a month, the return has remained unfiled after the due date or extension
      `a waiver applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure was due to circumstances beyond your control, or you filed every return on time in the previous five years and the Department had not contacted you for enforcement about this year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my late filing penalty` `the tax due for the year` `months or part months the return was late` `a waiver applies` MEANS
    `the late filing penalty` `the tax due for the year` `months or part months the return was late` `a waiver applies`
